### Assessment
- All 12 point estimates match within rounding tolerance (max difference: 0.0005)
- County counts match exactly: 87 (Dem turnout), 126 (vote share, turnout), 58 (VBM share)
- Standard errors are very close; minor differences in the quadratic VBM share SE (0.085 vs 0.076) likely reflect finite-sample correction differences between Stata's `reghdfe` and our implementation
- **Qualitative conclusions are identical to the original paper**

### Discrepancies
- No substantive discrepancies. All differences are within numerical precision of the 3-decimal-place reporting in the original paper.
- The minor SE difference in Table 3 col 6 (quadratic VBM share) is the largest discrepancy. This is a highly saturated model (58 county FE + 10 state-year FE + 58 county linear trends + 58 county quadratic trends, with only 580 observations), so small numerical differences in the projection algorithm are expected.

### Code
The replication code is in `code/02_replicate.py`. It uses iterative demeaning (alternating projections) to absorb multi-way fixed effects, then computes OLS on residuals with clustered standard errors at the county level.

